  "body": "What: Add a corner relief option for closed 2D pocket and slot boundaries. Choices: none, dogbone, T-bone (direction chosen per corner or by a rule). The toolpath cuts the relief so a square mating part fits. Verification stays inside the stock and the cutter radius.\n\nWhy: A round cutter cannot cut a square inside corner. Router products offer Normal, Dog-Bone and T-Bone fillets (Vectric) and automatic dogbones (CloudCut). #2161 only warns about tight corners.\n\nSources: https://docs.vectric.com/docs/V9.0/VCarvePro/ENU/Help/VCarvePro.pdf , https://cloudcut.cam/\n\nPart of #2395. Changes toolpath geometry, so effort:high. Must not gouge: relief stays inside the part boundary rules.\n\nDone means: a pocket with square corners generates a golden CL with the relief, a gouge check passes, and a refusal test covers a corner that the cutter cannot reach.\n",
